// PLAYTEST: how bad is the deep Stack now?
//
// `Stack depth 5 may be unwinnable` has been an open question since
// 2026-08-08, diagnosed then as a scaling problem rather than a gear or
// roster one: zone and depth multipliers compound, 4x zone by 3.32x depth
// is 13.3x at zone 3 depth 5, and no species stat can fix a multiplier.
//
// The trained policy makes it worse. The nearest training scenario,
// `08-rolled-stack` at depth *3*, went from 80% to 92% enemy win rate. This
// is the same shape two frames deeper, and it is here so the decision about
// that scaling is made against what the game now actually does rather than
// against last week's numbers.
//
// A rolled encounter rather than an authored one on purpose: the question
// is what the Stack *generates*, not what someone can compose.
//
// What to watch: is there a line of play that wins this, or is every round
// forced? If nothing you do changes the outcome, the answer is not
// `ENEMY_POLICY_TEMPERATURE` — a policy dialled back far enough to matter
// here is a policy switched off — it is the zone x depth curve.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 20, zone: 3),
    equip: [
        (item: "plasma_router", tier: 0),
        (item: "bastion_lattice", tier: 0),
        (item: "singularity_matrix", tier: 0),
    ],
    party: [
        (species: "scrapper", level: 14),
        (species: "sentinel", level: 14),
        (species: "construct", level: 14),
    ],
    encounter: Some(Stack(biome: NullSector, depth: 5)),
    reps: 1,
    seed: 902,
)
